  "notes": [
    "scaffolded from freedos on 2026-09-13, then re-pointed at a 1989 ISA PC: qemu-system-i386 -machine isapc -cpu 486 -m 16, TCG, no NIC, pointer none.",
    "Boot media trap: SCO Xenix floppies carry no 0x55AA signature at offset 510 and the boot sector compares a 14-byte filename string at 0x1F8 that runs THROUGH 0x1FE/0x1FF. Patch both bytes: 55 AA at 510 AND 0x0e -> 0x06 at offset 121 (the compare length).",
    "Media trap: WinWorld 386 2.3.4q is a MIXED set (Installation = typ=386PS MicroChannel, utilities = typ=n386 2.3.4h). The 386PS kernel panics with TRAP 8 under QEMU. Use the PCjs typ=386GT rel=2.3.4h N1/N2 floppies, which boot to init.",
    "retronet OPEN: SCO TCP/IP for Xenix is a separate product; no NIC in the device set and no rn-tapnet.sh committed (AGENTS.md rule 15)."
  ]
